+| M-SCOPE-center | For compact on-site G and a D2 vacuum alpha, xi↦omega_alpha(q(xi)) is Ad(H_alpha)-invariant and vanishes on [h_alpha,h_alpha]; nonzero tail-density jumps descend to `Lie(Z_{α,eff}^0)`. A Weyl representative with beta=n_w·alpha!=alpha and Ad_(n_w^-1)xi=-xi supplies an opposite-density A2 kink pair. Semisimple unbroken directions and finite groups supply no D13-calibrated memory. | SKETCH | D2, D9, D10, A2, M-quant-G, S-IDX-fin-G, S-IDX-G-label | compact-g-memory-scope.md §§1,3--4 | scope_g_check.py SG-C1 (finite covariance only) |
